{"_meta":{"com.oxinsider/docs-group":"traders","securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Get trader"},"description":"Look up a prediction market trader by wallet address or username. Returns grade (S through F), the edge over the price paid the profile badge shows (price_edge), and the sports and esports record: realized P&L (pnl.in_scope), markets traded, win rate, and volume. Wallet figures cover sports and esports markets only.\n\nOptional expand fields for heavier data:\n- strategy: Trading strategy classification\n- categories: Per-category performance breakdown\n- quant_metrics: retired since 2026-10-27; accepted and never returned, because its metrics covered every market of the wallet. Read pnl.in_scope or get_trader_pnl for the sports and esports record\n- trust: Per-field provenance (source, freshness, reconciliation, completeness) for grade, P&L, and stats\n- breakdowns: The profile's strategy breakdowns over sports and esports markets: P&L and win rate by UTC hour of first trade, hold-time and hour-of-day bands, risk metrics with category concentration, and entry-price buckets with their coverage (the settled positions the buckets leave out, such as two-sided hedges, by reason, count and P&L; its per-market P&L sum differs from pnl.in_scope.realized_pnl, which is Polymarket's published figure). Computed on the request, so slower for large wallets\n\nA wallet address with no trader yet returns sync_status \"unknown\" (not an error). A username or trader id that matches no trader is a not_found error.\n\nArgs:\n  - address (string, required): Ethereum wallet address (0x...) or trader username\n  - expand (string[], optional): Heavy fields to include: \"strategy\", \"categories\", \"trust\", \"breakdowns\" (\"quant_metrics\" is accepted and returns nothing)\n  - max_age_s (integer, optional, 0 or more): Freshness ceiling in seconds. The call answers only when data_quality.status is fresh or stale and data_quality.as_of is no older than this; otherwise it fails with reason freshness_ceiling_unsatisfied (HTTP 409). Nothing is refreshed to meet it\n\nReturns: Trader profile with grade, P&L, stats, and optional expanded fields. The trader carries data_quality: status, as_of (the oldest clock the body rests on) and field_groups. fresh and stale both mean tracked and clocked; stale means as_of is older than max_age_s, the refresh budget of the group writer. Neither is a tolerance: compare as_of with your own. unknown means this read cannot date that group, never that it is recent.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"address":{"description":"Ethereum wallet address (0x...) or trader username","maxLength":100,"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"expand":{"description":"Optional heavy fields to include; breakdowns adds the profile's hourly performance, hold-time and hour bands, risk metrics with category concentration, and entry-price buckets, computed on the request","items":{"enum":["strategy","categories","quant_metrics","trust","breakdowns"],"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"max_age_s":{"description":"Freshness ceiling in seconds: answer only when data_quality.status is fresh or stale and data_quality.as_of is no older than this, otherwise fail with freshness_ceiling_unsatisfied","minimum":0,"type":"integer"}},"required":["address"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_trader","outputSchema":{"$defs":{"AnalyticInteger":{"properties":{"freshness_at":{"format":"date-time","type":"string"},"source":{"enum":["provider","insert_time","cache","computed"],"type":"string"},"state":{"enum":["computed","known_zero","not_computed","not_applicable","stale","unavailable","insufficient_data"],"type":"string"},"value":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["state","source"],"type":"object"},"AnalyticNumber":{"properties":{"freshness_at":{"format":"date-time","type":"string"},"source":{"enum":["provider","inse